{% extends 'pages/communities/sagamok/members-first-plan-layout.html.twig' %}
{% set plan_key = 'health' %}{% set plan_short = 'Health, families and Elders' %}{% set plan_eyebrow = 'Priority 5' %}
{% set plan_title = 'Health, families and Elders supported close to home' %}
{% set plan_description = 'Organize care around members, connect services across departments and make access, referrals, follow-up and unmet need visible.' %}
{% block plan_content %}
<section><header><p class="plan-kicker">The outcome</p><h2>One front door, warm hand-offs and fewer people lost between services.</h2><p class="plan-lede">Members should not have to understand the organization chart to get help. A navigator owns the hand-off until the next service accepts it.</p></header><div class="plan-grid plan-grid--3"><div class="plan-card"><h3>Easy access</h3><p>One current service map, contact route and response standard.</p></div><div class="plan-card"><h3>Continuity</h3><p>Referrals close only when the member reaches the next service.</p></div><div class="plan-card"><h3>Care close to home</h3><p>Invest first in prevention, home support and culturally safe local care.</p></div></div></section>
<section><header><p class="plan-kicker">Year One commitments</p><h2>Build a coordinated care system.</h2></header><div class="plan-commitments"><article class="plan-commitment"><h3>Community service map</h3><p>Publish services, eligibility, contact points, hours, response targets and outside referrals.</p></article><article class="plan-commitment"><h3>Member navigation</h3><p>Create one route for health, mental wellness, addictions, family support, income and housing referrals.</p></article><article class="plan-commitment"><h3>Elders-at-home plan</h3><p>Coordinate home support, meals, transport, accessibility, medicines, visits and caregiver relief.</p></article><article class="plan-commitment"><h3>Youth wellness pathway</h3><p>Connect early help, crisis response, culture, recreation, school and clinical services.</p></article><article class="plan-commitment"><h3>After-hours standard</h3><p>State what help is available, who responds and how urgent needs move to the right provider.</p></article><article class="plan-commitment"><h3>Unmet-needs report</h3><p>Aggregate waits, declined referrals, service gaps and outside-care dependence without member PII.</p></article></div></section>
<section><header><p class="plan-kicker">Quarterly measures</p><h2>Measure access and continuity.</h2></header><div class="plan-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Access</th><th>Continuity</th><th>Elders</th><th>Youth and families</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Response and appointment times</td><td>Referrals accepted and completed</td><td>Members receiving home supports and wait time</td><td>Early-help access and completed follow-up</td></tr><tr><td>Requests unresolved after standard</td><td>Repeat intake caused by failed hand-off</td><td>Transport, meals and caregiver-support gaps</td><td>Crisis follow-up within the adopted standard</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section>
<section class="plan-decision"><h2>Decisions members make</h2><ul><li>Which services are hardest to reach now?</li><li>What should the Nation guarantee close to home?</li><li>What supports let Elders remain safely at home longer?</li><li>Which aggregate outcomes can be reported without compromising privacy?</li></ul></section>
<div class="plan-next"><a href="/communities/sagamok/members-first-plan/homes-infrastructure">← Homes and infrastructure</a><a href="/communities/sagamok/members-first-plan/language-culture-learning">Next: Language, culture and learning →</a></div>
{% endblock %}
